Source: tinhmenhdo-ubuntu
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: TinhMenhDo Ubuntu maintainers <vuquyettam@gmail.com>
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tinhmenhdo-ubuntu
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, vanilla-gnome-desktop, gnome-session, gnome-software, gnome-software-plugin-flatpak, flatpak
Conflicts: snapd, snapd-desktop-integration, gnome-software-plugin-snap
Breaks: snapd, snapd-desktop-integration, gnome-software-plugin-snap
Description: TinhMenhDo Ubuntu vanilla GNOME and Flatpak metapackage
 TinhMenhDo Ubuntu configures an Ubuntu desktop around the vanilla GNOME
 desktop packages, GNOME Software and Flatpak. It conflicts with snapd so
 APT cannot keep snapd installed alongside this profile.
 .
 This package deliberately does not purge user data, call apt recursively,
 add third-party repositories, or install a browser from a PPA.
